    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n100879" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύνορθρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dawning along with</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥξει σύνορθρον αὐγαῖς</span>
			<i>dawning with</i> the first beams of day, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				254
			</span></i> (lyr.), as restored by Wellauer and <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύνορθον αὐταῖς</span>: two
			codd. give <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύναρθρον</span>.</div>
